From: Parcel Play OS <kernel@parcel.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] libbpf: preserve const qualifier while scanning search path

GCC 15 diagnoses assignment of strchr() on a const input to a mutable pointer
when the Ubuntu Generic BTF tools are built with warnings as errors. The path
is never modified, so preserve the qualifier.

--- a/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
+++ b/tools/lib/bpf/libbpf.c
@@
-			char *next_path;
+			const char *next_path;
